          "filename": "White Ladies Priory (9287750308).jpg",
          "caption": "White Ladies Priory, once the Priory of St Leonard at Brewood, was an English priory of Augustinian canonesses, now in ruins, in Shropshire. Dissolved in 1536, it became famous for its role in the escape of Charles II of England after the Battle of Worcester in 1651. The timber priory buildings have long vanished and what is left is the Priory church walls.",
